Feature: Daily Swing with Weekly Channel Filter
  Primary timeframe: 1d
  Parameter oversold default 35
  Parameter overbought default 65
  Parameter stop_loss_pct default 5
  Parameter take_profit_pct default 12

  # Multi-timeframe (daily primary, weekly background): buy daily RSI dips while
  # price holds above the 8-week low, sell RSI spikes while price is capped under
  # the 8-week high. The weekly channel (highest_high / lowest_low on 1w) and the
  # weekly EMA trend are resolved lookahead-safely from the most recently CLOSED
  # weekly bar. Two charts render per trade — the daily entry/exit and the weekly
  # context.

  Background:
    Given a series weekly_high defined as highest_high(8) on 1w
    And a series weekly_low defined as lowest_low(8) on 1w

  Scenario: Enter long on an oversold dip holding the weekly channel
    Given no open position
    When rsi_oversold(oversold)
    And close is above weekly_low
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 + take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit long on an overbought spike
    Given a long position is open
    When rsi_overbought(overbought)
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Enter short on an overbought spike capped by the weekly channel
    Given no open position
    When rsi_overbought(overbought)
    And close is below weekly_high
    Then short_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 + stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 - take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit short on an oversold dip
    Given a short position is open
    When rsi_oversold(oversold)
    Then short_exit
